      "updated_at": "2025-02-08T09:24:38Z",
      "body": "> Sure! Having another thought, then maybe not change Overlapped_Clear() to take a PyObject *, i.e. keep it unchanged and all of its occurrences wouldn't have to be touched and the PR could be kept smaller?\r\n\r\nNo that's the problem of the PR. The signature of the clear function must be `int (*)(PyObject *)` and not `int (*)(OverlappedObject *)`. What I'm trying to fix are undefined behaviours reported by clang (currently, those are suppressed because we are adding an explicit cast, but we don't want that to be kept)",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
